# PlatformIO
.pio
.pioenvs
.piolibdeps
.clang_complete
.gcc-flags.json

# VS Code: ignore every file/folder directly under .vscode by default so local/editor-generated junk does not get committed.
.vscode/*

# VS Code: re-include the .vscode directory itself so Git can consider carefully whitelisted shared files below.
!.vscode/

# VS Code: include recommended extensions only; this is portable repo guidance for contributors and dev agents.
!.vscode/extensions.json

# VS Code: include shared workspace settings only if this file is manually curated and contains portable repo-level settings.
!.vscode/settings.json

# VS Code / PlatformIO: explicitly ignore generated debug configs because they can contain absolute clone paths and user-local toolchain paths.
.vscode/launch.json

# VS Code / PlatformIO C/C++: explicitly ignore generated IntelliSense config because PlatformIO generates it with absolute paths.
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json

# VS Code: keep shared task definitions ignored until/unless we intentionally create a portable tasks.json using relative paths.
.vscode/tasks.json

# VS Code local overrides: keep personal settings files ignored if a developer/agent creates them.
.vscode/*.local.json

# VS Code local overrides: keep any other local-only .vscode config variants ignored.
.vscode/*.local.*

# VS Code C/C++: ignore IntelliSense precompiled-header cache.
.vscode/ipch/

# VS Code C/C++: ignore generated symbol/browse database files.
.vscode/browse.VC.db*

# VS Code/extensions: ignore local extension caches.
.vscode/.cache/

# VS Code/extensions: ignore local edit/history artifacts created by history extensions or tooling.
.vscode/.history/

# VS Code/testing: ignore generated test result artifacts if any tool writes them under .vscode.
.vscode/test-results/

# VS Code/testing: ignore generated coverage artifacts if any tool writes them under .vscode.
.vscode/coverage/

